}_{2}-{\\text{proj}}_{{v}_{1}}{a}_{2} \\\\  & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{{a}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{v}_{1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]-(\\frac{4}{2})[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]-2[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we normalize ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{q}_{1} & =\\frac{{v}_{1}}{‖{v}_{1}‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {q}_{2} & =\\frac{{v}_{2}}{‖{v}_{2}‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we compute $R:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R & ={Q}^{T}\\,A \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{2} & 2\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we obtain the following QR factorization of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\overset{A}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}]}}=\\overset{Q}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}0 & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\end{aligned}]}}\\overset{R}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{2} & 2\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}]}}.\n$$\n\nFinally, ${q}_{31}\\cdot {r}_{12}=(-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}})\\cdot (2\\sqrt{2})=-2.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388793 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388794 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388793 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388795 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388793 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388796 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388793 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388797 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [1